{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And you shall say: moreover, here is your servant Jacob behind us.</b> Repeat this statement — even when you see him, do not be afraid to say this thing to him. And if he asks you: what is this, that he did not go ahead to meet me? He should have gone out and come forward, for he is my younger brother. And you shall answer him: <b>for he said</b> Jacob — I will appease his face and calm the anger he has toward me with the gift going before me, and afterward I will see his face; perhaps he will show me favor. Another interpretation: <b>for he said: I will appease his face</b> — the master of the book (i.e., the author of the verse) explained this matter, but the emissaries did not say it, for if so, they would themselves recall to Esau the hatred and enmity."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:07.096546870Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}